{"key":"apcalcab-mcq-070","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"6","working":"To estimate lim(x->2) f(x) from the table, we examine the behavior of f(x) as x approaches 2 from both sides. As x approaches 2 from the left (x = 1.9, 1.99, 1.999), f(x) takes values 5.9, 5.99, 5.999, which approach 6. As x approaches 2 from the right (x = 2.1, 2.01, 2.001), f(x) takes values 6.1, 6.01, 6.001, which also approach 6. Since both one-sided limits appear to approach 6, the limit as x approaches 2 is estimated to be 6. The value of f(2) is not required to find the limit.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":466,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":466,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":615,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":227,"reasoningTokens":388},"totalTokens":1081,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":388,"promptTokenCount":466,"candidatesTokenCount":227,"totalTokenCount":1081,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":466}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":227}]},"reasoningTokens":388,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":6059,"keyed_label":"C"}
