{"key":"apcalcab-mcq-022","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"B","final_answer":"1","working":"For f to be continuous at x = 2, the left-hand limit, right-hand limit, and function value at x = 2 must all be equal. We compute: lim(x->2-) f(x) = lim(x->2-) (kx + 1) = 2k + 1. The right-hand limit and function value are f(2) = lim(x->2+) f(x) = lim(x->2+) (x^2 - 1) = 2^2 - 1 = 3. Setting the two equal gives 2k + 1 = 3, which implies 2k = 2, so k = 1.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":383,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":383,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":383,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":186,"reasoningTokens":197},"totalTokens":766,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":197,"promptTokenCount":383,"candidatesTokenCount":186,"totalTokenCount":766,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":383}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":186}]},"reasoningTokens":197,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4889,"keyed_label":"B"}
